<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jiaozhi Province</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1407–1427</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiaozhi">Jiaozhi</a> Province was the Ming Chinese province created in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor">Yongle Emperor</a>'s armies overthrew the Hồ dynasty in 1407, reviving an old Han-era name. Ming rule brought heavy taxation and efforts at cultural assimilation and provoked repeated revolts. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lam-son-uprising">Lam Sơn uprising</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-loi">Lê Lợi</a> forced the Ming to withdraw in 1427, restoring Vietnamese independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jiaozhi-province.jpg" alt="Jiaozhi Province" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leeaan · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Jiaozhi_Province_of_the_Ming_Dynasty_(vi).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
